
==============================================================================
P1  R1 frame-overdetermination: frame(net) = frame(drift) = frame(noise)?
==============================================================================
  A  common supplied site frame: overlap(net frame, drift axes) = 1.000000; overlap(net frame, noise axes) = 1.000000
  B  drift written on-site in an independently rotated frame (admissible: V convex, gradient flow well posed):
     overlap(net frame, drift axes) = 0.3492; overlap(rotated frame, drift axes) = 1.000000
     rotated-drift model relaxes: |x(20)| = 6.87e-04 (from |x(0)| = 4.15)
     -> nothing earned forbids the independent rotation; agreement exists only because the declarations share a frame.
  C  comparator: an ordinary nonlinear Langevin network x' = -K x - grad V4 + xi with site-local V4 and site-local noise
     has the same frame agreement by construction (identical equations). -> CONSISTENCY-ONLY / STANDARD-STRUCTURE

