  static identity in ANY quadratic network (multi-site system S, equal T, product of the two Gibbs marginals):
   random network 0: E_S(prod) - E_S(Gibbs) = -1.112204;  (1/2)<E_int>_G = -1.112204
   random network 1: E_S(prod) - E_S(Gibbs) = -1.064791;  (1/2)<E_int>_G = -1.064791
   random network 2: E_S(prod) - E_S(Gibbs) = -0.868788;  (1/2)<E_int>_G = -0.868788
  -> the 1/2 is the quadratic-network equipartition identity (STANDARD); r is model-specific (kappa, g, c);
     the sign flips for alpha > 1/2 (INPUT-DEPENDENT).

